    "insights": [
      "The stated inequality |d(x0,xn)-d(y,xn)| <= d(x0,y)+sum d(xi,xi+1) is trivially true because the 3-point reverse inequality already gives <= d(x0,y); the nonneg chain sum only slackens it. The genuinely substantive theorem is the plain telescoping form |d(f0,w)-d(fn,w)| <= sum d(fi,fi+1), the reverse companion of the polygon inequality dist_le_range_sum_dist.",
